wn facts. So we should discuss D, compare with C, and maybe adjust recommendation.\n\nThus we can say: I see D's strong concentration and problem solving as critical for attention and decision quality, and his responsibility is high, but his moody and loner traits raise concerns for crew cooperation. However, C's egocentric and communication issues may be more detrimental. I think D might be a better overall fit if we can mitigate mood issues. So I propose shifting provisional vote to D, pending clarification on his crew cooperation.\n\nWe need to reference facts: D can concentrate very well (attention), solves problems extremely well (decision quality), takes responsibility seriously (responsibility), but considered moody and a loner (crew cooperation concerns). C: 100% reliable (operational reliability), creates positive atmosphere (crew cooperation), makes correct decisions quickly (decision quality), but difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education (communication, adaptability). So we can argue D's strengths outweigh C's concerns.\n\nThus we will state provisional recommendation for D.\n\nWe must include METADATA_JSON with vote \"Candidate D\".\n\nProceed."}
